// Silkscreen as a bitmap font, one glyph per block.
// Bitmap conversion of Silkscreen (Copyright 2001 The Silkscreen Project Authors),
// SIL Open Font License 1.1: see OFL-Silkscreen.txt. Edit glyphs like sprites.
//
// Format: "height N" (rows per glyph), "baseline N" (rows above the baseline),
// then for each character a line "= X" ("= space" for a space) followed by
// exactly `height` rows of "#" (ink) and "." (clear). The row width is the
// glyph's advance, side bearings included. Lines starting with // are comments.

height 9
baseline 8

= space
